2026-10-01T23:38:57.7549527Z   describe content that is in NO COMMIT. A reader who checks out the `git_revision` this
2026-10-01T23:38:57.7550109Z   manifest names and verifies gets a mismatch on a file nobody can produce. That is not a
2026-10-01T23:38:57.7550946Z   staleness — the inventory may well be current — it is a provenance failure, and it is
2026-10-01T23:38:57.7551430Z   why this is refused rather than reported as STALE.
2026-10-01T23:38:57.7551949Z   ⭐ THE FIX IS AN ORDERING, NOT A REGENERATION, AND REGENERATING NOW MAKES IT WORSE.
2026-10-01T23:38:57.7552530Z   Running `python3 research/manuscripts/aso_archive_manifest.py` against the tree you have
2026-10-01T23:38:57.7553408Z   right now re-hashes the same uncommitted edits and writes `false` again — that is the
2026-10-01T23:38:57.7554208Z   obvious response to a STALE line and it is what produced the bad artifact on `main`.
2026-10-01T23:38:57.7554785Z   Instead: commit (or stash) every other change FIRST, then regenerate the manifest
2026-10-01T23:38:57.7555337Z   against the clean tree as the session's LAST commit. Same generator, same inputs; only
2026-10-01T23:38:57.7555873Z   the ordering differs, and the ordering is the whole content of this field.
